From 25eecfe3f2d07b5fbf68d85a01eef63ac0d93fdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:28:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drivers/net: add the ZX279128S Ethernet driver (E2)

Wire the block programmed by the previous two commits into the U-Boot
network stack.  The device tree node is probed, the PHY behind lan1
(MDIO address 12) is connected and started, and the MAC and the traffic
manager are left ready for the first frame.

The frame path is polled: the BMU hands out 2048-byte buffers by index,
send/recv move one descriptor at a time through the fixed 16 MiB DMA
arena at 0x45000000, and free_pkt returns both the RX slot and its
buffer.  The arena is not allocated at runtime because the traffic
manager tables, the descriptor rings and the buffer pool must all sit
inside it; U-Boot owns no memory in that range otherwise.

Because the arena is live while the network runs, e2631flash now refuses
a RAM source that overlaps it, and e2631verify reports the same refusal
instead of comparing traffic manager data.  e2631_net_refclk_init() is
made idempotent so the driver can call it from start() even when
e2631boot already ran it; the register sequence is unchanged.

The e2631net command prints the driver state for a console session.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/zx279128s-zte-zxhn-e2631.dts  |  35 +-
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631flash.c          |  58 +++-
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631net.c            |  11 +
 configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig |   6 +
 drivers/net/zx279128s_eth.c                | 383 +++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 480 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

